<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24423" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημοκρᾰτ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for a democracy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					338e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημοκρατικόν τι δρᾶν</span> to do
			a <i>popular</i> act, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				952
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δίκαιον τὸ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1280a9
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					2.32
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				6.3.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημοτικός</span> is more usu. in this
			sense), <i>favouring democracy</i> or <i>suited to democracy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				25.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				571a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1131a27
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
